# Extract the personal stroke vocabulary

## Scope and existing evidence

Historical notes below identify existing domain primitives but do not prove
that the proposed finite synthesis contract is executable.

Derive centerlines, contours, entry and exit conditions, pen lifts, ligatures,
diacritics, contextual forms, and confidence with sample provenance.

Current executable evidence now freezes the transport-neutral vocabulary entry
produced by later extraction. Each entry retains caller-owned centerline and
contour evidence, entry/exit conditions, pen-lift evidence, ligature, diacritic,
and contextual-form evidence, plus confidence and sample provenance. Extraction,
geometry/units, form inference, confidence calculation, profile-section schema,
and candidate generation remain open.

## Finite provenance-linked core stroke vocabulary contract

**Inputs:** one explicitly accepted, corrected calibration capture, stable
profile ID `student-A`, source sample IDs and typed observed stroke evidence.
**Outputs:** one finite proposed vocabulary per declared role: centerline,
contour bounds, entry/exit tangents, pen contacts/lifts, diacritic attachments,
contextual variants, confidence status and original evidence links. Proposed
vocabulary records are not automatically accepted glyph coverage.

**Core role sample ledger (theoretical):**

| Role / sample | Centerline and contour | Context / lift / mark |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Body `a`, `c01-A` | Points and contour | Standalone; one lift |
| Join `an`, `c02-A` | Paths and transition | Tangent; no lift at join |
| Title `B`, `c08-A` | Tall contour | Title; two lifts |
| Label `F`, `c09-A` | Compact contour | Label; one lift |
| Mark `ñ`, `c03-A` | Base plus tilde path | Anchor; mark lift |

**Provenance rule:** each derived centerline and contour retains the exact
capture and corrected region, physical unit in mm, calibration transform
revision and observed/inferred confidence. A pen lift is a categorical
contact transition rather than an invented stroke connecting two samples.
Entry and exit tangents belong to each contextual form, so the joined `a`
cannot silently replace isolated `a`. Derived accents are allowed only after
the profile's declared applicable rule admits that composition.

**Worked example:** `student-A` has corrected sample `c02-A` with an observed
joining exit from `a` to `n`; a proposed `a` form records its start and end
points, contour, `JoinedBeforeN` context, `PenDown` exit, provenance key
`capture-12/region-c02/revision-3` and confidence `Observed`. The isolated
`a` from `c01-A` is a separate contextual form and remains available for
word ends. Neither record claims synthesized ink exists until a planner
selects a compatible, non-colliding path.

**Refusal example:** sample `c08-A` has no corrected physical scale, or its
centerline lacks an exit contact state. It remains `UnresolvedVocabulary`
with the exact missing field instead of fabricating a usable title glyph.
An unknown source region, held-out sample masquerading as training, stale
transform, or unmeasured diacritic anchor similarly refuses extraction.

**Assumptions and limits:** typed vocabulary data structures already retain
these fields, but the algorithm for photo-to-stroke centerlines, contour
segmentation, tangents, join inference, confidence and real glyph selection
is not implemented. The five example records are theoretical evidence forms,
not digitized personal handwriting or universal language coverage.

## Acceptance decision

- **Basis:** practical for the typed vocabulary record and provenance fields;
  theoretical for actual stroke derivation and suitability, 2026-11-02.
- **Delivered:** five role/context records, source and confidence invariant,
  one joined-form example and incomplete-extraction refusal.
- **Not implemented by this acceptance:** raster extraction, profile writer
  training, automatic glyph selection, calibration quality or rendering.
